% Plastics rulings of U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CROSS, rulings.cbp.gov)
% run through the whole modelled tariff (tariff.le). The first prototype's
% sample of articles of plastics (see README.md).
%
% One scenario per ruling, which the scenario names ("scenario n is, as
% stated in ruling NY ...:"); each article is described by the facts the
% ruling states, each pointing at its passage ("confer "..."");
% the office's judgments — the principal use, the essential character of a
% composite good or set, the answer to a claim that the article belongs to a
% heading outside the model — say who made them. The ruling's code is NOT
% a fact: the expectation is the six-digit subheading the model derives.
% Selection: the most recent rulings returned by CROSS for 3923.21-90,
% 3924.10-90 and 3926.20-90 (September 2026). Rulings N360188-N360191 are one
% bag imported from four countries. See README.md for the method and results.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base plastics cbp includes these resources:
    tariff.

the knowledge base plastics cbp includes:

