% NY N358771 (February 2026): a lipstick container from South Korea.
scenario ny_n358771 is, as stated in ruling NY N358771:
    the lipstick container LPNR001 is a manufactured article,
        confer "described as a lipstick container, model number LPNR001, constructed from an injection-molded plastic".
    the lipstick container LPNR001 is made of plastics,
        confer "constructed from an injection-molded plastic".
    the principal use of the lipstick container LPNR001 is packing of goods,
        according to CBP, confer "designed to protect the contents from external impact and contamination, and to facilitate its transport, storage, and use".
    the lipstick container LPNR001 is shaped as cylindrical container,
        according to CBP, confer "The product is a cylindrical round container which is not considered a box",
        because "a cylindrical round container is not a box, case, crate or similar article".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the lipstick container LPNR001 is 3923.90"].

% NY N342911 (September 2024): WPP/BOPP bags from Dominican Republic-Central America.
scenario ny_n342911 is, as stated in ruling NY N342911:
    the WPP BOPP bag is a manufactured article,
        confer "(i) the good is a good wholly obtained or produced entirely in the territory of one or more of the parties to the Agreement".
    the WPP BOPP bag is made of plastics,
        confer "strips 2 mm wide and laminated with plastic visible to the naked eye and classified in heading 5903.".
    the WPP BOPP bag is shaped as sack,
        confer "on the status of WPP/BOPP bags from Dominican Republic-Central America under the DR-CAFTA".
    the WPP BOPP bag contains 100 percent of polypropylene,
        confer "described as a bag made from woven polypropylene (WPP) that is coated on the exterior with melted polypropylene laminated".
    the principal use of the WPP BOPP bag is packing of goods,
        according to CBP, confer "The bags are used for packaging products including animal feed".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the WPP BOPP bag is 3923.29"].
